thy: labs do not show acute hyper/hypoglycemia or electrolyte derangements specific to diabetes", "Infectious fever syndrome: while fever is present, blasts and constitutional symptoms suggest hematologic rather than infectious origin"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Neurological deficits (ataxia, visual changes)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.5911428097528613, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The high blast percentage and subacute course argue against typical chronic myeloproliferative phases (B2), moderately increasing support for acute myeloid pro…"], "evidence_against": ["The subacute constitutional symptoms are more typical of lymphoid neoplasms (B3), but the presence of myeloid blasts makes this less likely. This action modera…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.164, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The high blast percentage and subacute course argue against typical chronic myeloproliferative phases (B2), moderately increasing support for acute myeloid pro…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.058, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_